{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/867634-oath-of-the-axe","id":867634,"title":"Oath of the Axe","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-18T10:06:47-07:00","id":867634,"title":"Oath of the Axe","content":"Hi there. I have some questions regarding the Great Oath taken by members of the Sworn of the Axe:<br /> <br /> Just how much responsibility comes with it? I know that Axe Sworn must defend the Covenant as a whole, as well as deal with any leaks of covenant secrets, but must the Sworn of the Axe also be the babysitters of even the most junior and least powerful/knowledgable/influential members of the order?<br /> <br /> Are there times when it is OK for a member of the Axe, when faced with a junior member of her covenant being attacked and likely killed by powerful member of an outsider to say: &quot;I am more valuable than that slave/supplicant, and it does make sense to potentially sacrifice myself to save one such as they.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or is it more appropriate to say that a vampire who would utter such words is just not cut out to take the Oath of the Axe?<br /> <br /> What have been your experience with the Axe Sworn in your games? Whether as PCs, STs, or interacting with NPCs? Inquiring minds want to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:41:23-07:00","id":867654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/867634-oath-of-the-axe#post867634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but must the Sworn of the Axe also be the babysitters of even the most junior and least powerful/knowledgable/influential members of the order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no, absolutely. The Sworn of the Axe has ranks, too, after all. The low level Axe protect other low level guys, high level axe protect high level guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:15:11-07:00","id":868478,"title":"","content":"Under first edition rules, the Axe Sworn take a greater oath to willingly sacrifice their own life and limb to physically defend the covenant secrets AND their members. It's not their role to assign arbitrary values to individual members and decide from there whether or not they are worth defending. If said member was worth inducting, they're worth defending. If your character considers his own personal agendas as more valuable than the Ordo Dracul, then they really shouldn't be swearing a greater oath.<br /> If I were STing, if an Axe Sworn refused to defend another member for any reason, the best they could hope for would be expelled from the Greater Oath for cowardice. An Axe Sworn has multiple methods of dealing with junior covenant members seeking to use them as WMDs or professional hit men in purely personal feuds, the least of them being the covenant's hierarchy itself and propensity to delegate responsibilities. They can literally make the cost of &quot;hiring&quot; them too expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}